      "message": "To keep the iterator consistent, it would make sense to always update it  from the `next_node` result, even if it\u0027s `None` (so that repeated calls on `.next()` are guaranteed to return `None`, no matter what). For example:\n```\nlet (node, depth) \u003d self.node?;\nself.node \u003d node.next_node(depth).ok().flatten().filter(|(_, depth)| depth \u003e 0);\n\nself.node\n```",
